<title>CANADA: Key Toronto stock index hits record closing high.</title>
<headline>Key Toronto stock index hits record closing high.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>CHANGE				     CHANGE</p>
<p>TSE	5518.10    +25.50    HI 5518.30	LOW  5497.75</p>
<p>DJI	6090.87     -3.36    GOLD (LONDON)   US$381.00  +1.00</p>
<p>FTSE100  4073.10    +20.00    GOLD (NY-COMEX) US$383.60  +1.50</p>
<p>NIKKEI  21302.95   -309.35    LME CASH NICKEL US$6940    -91.0</p>
<p>CANDLR    1.3464		  LME CASH ALUM   US$1332.0   +4.0</p>
<p>CAN 30-YR 110.40     +0.51    NOV BRENT CRUDE US$24.65   +0.11</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>* Toronto stocks surged to close at a new index record, propelled by soaring golds &amp; oils. * Mergers, earnings kept turnover high at 858 million shares worth C$1.25 million.  </p>
<p>The key index of Canada's largest stock exchange broke through the psychological barrier of 5500 points on Monday and hit a new closing high of 5518 points.</p>
<p>The Toronto Stock Exchange's 300 Composite Index rose 25.5 points to hit 5518 by day's end, propelled higher by soaring gold issues and surging oil stocks.</p>
<p>The 300 Index reached 5000 on Feb. 1.</p>
<p>&quot;There seems... to be foreign interest in Canada,&quot; one trader said.</p>
